y or waxy bump, often with visible blood vessels','Flat, flesh-colored or brown scar-like lesion','Bleeding or scabbing sore that heals and recurs','Pink growth with raised edges and central indentation','Usually appears on sun-exposed areas (face, neck, hands)']},{name:'Actinic Keratoses',abbreviation:'AKIEC',riskLevel:'precancerous',description:'Actinic keratosis is a rough, scaly patch caused by years of sun exposure. It is considered precancerous and may develop into squamous cell carcinoma if untreated.',commonSigns:['Rough, dry, scaly patch of skin (less than 1 inch)','Flat or slightly raised reddish patch','Hard, wart-like surface','Itching, burning, or tenderness in the affected area','Appears on face, lips, ears, forearms, and scalp']},{name:'Melanocytic Nevi',abbreviation:'NV',riskLevel:'benign',description:'Commonly known as moles, melanocytic nevi are benign growths that form when melanocytes grow in clusters. Most moles are harmless but should be monitored for changes.',commonSigns:['Uniform round or oval shape','Consistent brown, tan, or black color throughout','Smooth, well-defined borders','Flat or slightly raised surface','Stable appearance over time (no changes)']},{name:'Benign Keratosis',abbreviation:'BKL',riskLevel:'benign',description:'Benign keratosis-like lesions include seborrheic keratoses and other harmless growths. They are non-cancerous and very common in older adults.',commonSigns:['Waxy, "stuck-on" appearance','Tan, brown, or black color, may vary','Well-defined, round or oval shape','Slightly raised, rough or warty surface','Can appear anywhere on the body']},{name:'Dermatofibroma',abbreviation:'DF',riskLevel:'benign',description:'Dermatofibromas are benign skin growths (fibrous nodules) most commonly found on the lower legs. They are generally harmless and require no treatment.',commonSigns:['Small, firm, raised nodule','Brownish, reddish-brown, or tan color','Dimpling or puckering when pinched (classic sign)','Often found on lower legs','Usually asymptomatic; may itch slightly']},{name:'Vascular Lesions',abbreviation:'VASC',riskLevel:'benign',description:'Vascular skin lesions are caused by abnormal blood vessels near the surface of the skin. Most are benign and range from cherry angiomas to port-wine stains.',commonSigns:['Bright red, purple, or blue color','Blanching (fading) when pressed firmly','Smooth surface, soft texture','Can range from tiny dots to larger flat patches','Common in adults over 30 (cherry angiomas)']}],l=[{dot:_r(d[5]).Colors.redDot,label:'High Risk',classes:'Melanoma, Basal Cell Carcinoma'},{dot:_r(d[5]).Colors.orangeDot,label:'Medium Risk',classes:'Actinic Keratoses'},{dot:_r(d[5]).Colors.greenDot,label:'Low Risk',classes:'Melanocytic Nevi, Benign Keratosis, Dermatofibroma, Vascular Lesions'}];_e.LesionGuideScreen=({navigation:e})=>{var h=(0,r.useState)(!1),p=(0,o.default)(h,2),y=p[0],u=p[1],b=e?.canGoBack?.();return(0,i.jsxs)(t.View,{style:c.container,children:[(0,i.jsx)(t.StatusBar,{barStyle:"light-content",backgroundColor:_r(d[5]).Colors.primary}),(0,i.jsxs)(t.View,{style:c.header,children:[b&&(0,i.jsx)(t.TouchableOpacity,{style:c.backBtn,onPress:()=>e.goBack(),activeOpacity:.75,children:(0,i.jsx)(t.Text,{style:c.backBtnText,children:"\u2190 Back"})}),(0,i.jsx)(t.Text,{style:c.headerTitle,children:"Pigmented Skin Lesion Guide"}),(0,i.jsx)(t.Text,{style:c.headerSubtitle,children:"Educational reference \xb7 Not for self-diagnosis"})]}),(0,i.jsxs)(t.ScrollView,{style:c.scroll,contentContainerStyle:c.scrollContent,showsVerticalScrollIndicator:!1,children:[(0,i.jsx)(t.View,{style:c.noticeCard,children:(0,i.jsx)(t.Text,{style:c.noticeText,children:"This guide is for educational purposes only. The ABCDE method and lesion descriptions below are reference material and do not replace professional medical diagnosis."})}),(0,i.jsxs)(t.TouchableOpacity,{style:c.abcdeHeader,onPress:()=>u(e=>!e),activeOpacity:.85,children:[(0,i.jsxs)(t.View,{style:c.abcdeTitleRow,children:[(0,i.js